      "name": "translation-adjudication",
      "title": "Translation adjudication — the review loop",
      "description": "A person's word on a translation, carried from the translation review page or a block's 🌐 pane to the record: anyone proposes text, which joins the ranked candidates; an owner, member or collaborator adjudicates, by accepting a catalogue or choosing one string's translation with a reason; it is filed as a `translation-adjudication/v1` issue; a workflow checks the author and the catalogue's hash, writes the records, re-runs the auto-pick and opens a PR; a maintainer merges it. Use for \"review the translations\", \"this string is mistranslated\", \"why was my review not recorded\", and when wiring a layer for review. Locale sign-off is a separate act, not this one.",
